<title>FRANCE: Legrand sees no significant rise in 96 results.</title>
<headline>Legrand sees no significant rise in 96 results.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Electrical company Legrand said on Wednesday it saw no significant rise in its results in 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;It does not seem very likely to us to foresee a significant increase in the 1996 result compared to 1995,&quot; finance director Oliver Bazil told a news conference.</p>
<p>For this to happen, the downturn in economic activity seen in France since the start of the year would have to end quickly, he said.</p>
<p>In the first half of 1996, Legrand's net profit fell 3.2 percent to 453 million francs.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
